I haven't tried. I was going to give it a day and see what the automated systems do. qpdf's CI runs pikepdf's test suite from pikepdf's main, so current pikepdf should work with current qpdf. pikepdf upstream watches qpdf carefully, and we are in regular communication. I haven't checked the others, but they use qpdf in a fairly straightforward way, and the API changes were all in dark corners of qpdf's tokenizer and so forth...not stuff the other packages would be likely to ever have to touch. All API changes were to functions that were deprecated for a long time, so there would be no surprises.

I'll keep an eye on things over the next couple of days.
